  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef pytorch_rnn_cell_from_scratch(x: list, h_prev: list, W_ih: list, W_hh: list, b_ih: list, b_hh: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **RNN Cell from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_rnn_cell_from_scratch(x: list, h_prev: list, W_ih: list, W_hh: list, b_ih: list, b_hh: list) -> list:\n    xt, hp = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(h_prev, dtype=torch.float32)\n    hn = torch.tanh(torch.matmul(torch.tensor(W_ih, dtype=torch.float32), xt) + torch.tensor(b_ih, dtype=torch.float32) + torch.matmul(torch.tensor(W_hh, dtype=torch.float32), hp) + torch.tensor(b_hh, dtype=torch.float32))\n    return np.round(hn.numpy(), 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
